      <h2>Right now, someone in your area<br>is searching for a <span style="color:var(--amber-dark)">tradie like you.</span><br>They're calling your competitor.</h2>
      <p>Here's a fact that'll sting a bit: <strong>nearly three-quarters</strong> of New Zealanders say a business's website is the most important way they engage with it. They Google your trade, your suburb, and they make a decision fast. If you don't have a website — or yours looks like it was built in 2009 — they're gone. They called someone else. Someone who might be worse than you at the actual job.</p>
      <p>We know what you're thinking. "Most of my work comes through word of mouth." It probably does. And word of mouth is great — until it dries up. Until a mate retires. Until a good customer moves away. Until you want to grow and realise you've got no way to reach people who've never heard of you.</p>
      <p><strong>47%</strong> of NZ small businesses have no website at all. Among sole traders, that number hits <strong>75%</strong>. Three out of four tradies in your area are invisible to anyone searching Google. That's not a crisis — that's an opportunity. But only for the tradies who act first.</p>
      <p>Here's the other thing: social media isn't the answer. Facebook is not a website. Instagram is not a website. You don't own either of them, you can't rank on Google with them, and they show your competitors' ads next to your work. A .nz domain with your name, your work and a way to contact you is the thing that's actually yours.</p>
      <p>That's exactly what WFT builds. Done for you. In 7 working days. For a flat NZ$1,997 — with a guarantee that would make every other web agency in New Zealand very nervous.</p>
